# Neon endpoint identity — the single machine-readable source of truth (D-05, D-05a).
#
# docs/operations/neon-branch-routing.md § Lifecycle is the human-readable
# counterpart of this file. Change both together whenever a branch is
# recreated or a new one is added.
#
# Format: one record per non-comment, non-blank line, exactly four
# `|`-separated fields, no spaces padding the separator:
#
#   prefix|hostname|branch|scope
#
#   prefix   — the endpoint id without the `-pooler...` suffix, used for
#              startsWith prefix matching.
#   hostname — the full pooled DNS name, used for exact-equality matching.
#   branch   — exactly one of: main, preview, development.
#   scope    — human-readable label, e.g. `PRODUCTION (Neon branch \`main\`)`.
#
# bug_011 discipline: match on URL.hostname, NEVER URL.host — `host` carries
# the port, so a connection string with an explicit `:5432` would slip a
# prefix match that was checking `host` instead of `hostname`. In bash the
# equivalent discipline is stripping at `/` OR `:` before comparing
# (see scripts/check-local-db-branch.sh).
#
# Consumers derive their own severity from the `branch` field. This file
# carries no per-consumer policy — it is pure data.
#
# FAIL-SAFE: an endpoint id that does NOT appear in this file must be
# treated as PRODUCTION by every consumer (see scripts/_neon-target.ts's
# `branch: 'unknown'` + `isProductionSeverity: true` handling).
ep-icy-boat-alx5o1tz|ep-icy-boat-alx5o1tz-pooler.c-3.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech|main|PRODUCTION (Neon branch `main`)
ep-delicate-night-als4ogpc|ep-delicate-night-als4ogpc-pooler.c-3.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech|preview|PREVIEW (Neon branch `preview`)
ep-polished-band-alphc576|ep-polished-band-alphc576-pooler.c-3.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech|development|DEVELOPMENT (Neon branch `development`)
